WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:09.760
To fight against messengers from the future who are changing history to erase soccer...

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.410
...we, the Raimon Eleven, are now traveling through time to assemble the strongest eleven in history.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.070
The year is 1554 A.D.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.800
23rd year of the Tembun Era.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.810
Location: Owari Province.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.800
We're here.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.730
The air smells great!

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.260
Well, c'mon! Let's head to the village!

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:21.750
Yeah!

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.700
It may be a bad idea to just wander in there.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.620
Certainly! With the way you're dressed, you'll stick out like sore thumbs!

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:29.760
Therefore!

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.080
Wondeba Switch On!

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.360
This is beautiful!

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.720
Now we kind of look the part!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.220
Nishiki-senpai, it suits you!

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.210
You think so?

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.500
I agree!

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.110
They look a little modern-ish though, don't you think?

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:53.350
Mmhm...

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:56.050
I kind of agree...

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.210
Will we be okay, Wondeba-san?

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.630
It'll be fine! Don't worry about it.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:05.680
Anyway, we should hide the caravan before someone sees it.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:07.200
Oh, that's right.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.190
Wondeba Switch On!

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.500
It disappeared!

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.540
I just made it invisible.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:19.400
Now, let's go check out the village!

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.750
So this is the old Japan...

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.050
Look, look! It's like being on the set of a period drama!

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:35.830
This is about as good as the set for that famous show "The Eleven Samurai Ninjas!"

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.220
They sure went full-scale!

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.920
I don't think "full-scale" is the right way to put it.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.690
Midori-san, you're very knowledgeable about history.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.180
She's just a huge nerd when it comes to samurai movies.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:46.940
What was that?!

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:47.610
Now, now.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.750
We've really come to Nobunaga's time.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.160
It's a little hard to believe.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.840
So, how will we get to meet Nobunaga?

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.460
Um, well...

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:02.820
Let's all split up and gather information.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:03.980
Agreed!

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.520
Okay everyone, time to investigate!

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.010
It's a boat!

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.450
Let's take a closer look, Shinsuke!

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:13.420
Tenma!

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.340
This looks great!

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.720
I guess you wouldn't know any place where Nobunaga would go, huh?

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.360
Sir, you need to pay.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.050
Nobunaga-sama, eh?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.490
He's never come here.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.450
I see.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.200
Anything from the Aura Radar?

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.690
Nope.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:40.250
We won't be able to follow Nobunaga unless we know what his aura noise is, anyway.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:46.430
It says that Nobunaga often appeared in the town around the castle.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.130
There should be some clues in the village.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.460
Forgive me!

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.440
I-It's okay.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.440
Forgive me!

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.840
Oh, just look at what I've done...

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.770
I'll have them dried at once.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.770
Please, come inside.

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.990
No, I'm in a hurry.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.100
You mustn't!

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.750
You'll catch a cold!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.750
Mother!

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.620
What's wrong?

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.380
Oh, is this a friend?

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.470
Come in.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.650
Please bear with this for the moment.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.960
Don't worry, it's been washed.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.150
No, that's not really...

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.570
That's...

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.450
Could that be soccer?

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.250
The people in this time period play soccer, too!

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.050
Let's check it out!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.240
Hey, is that soccer?

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:56.790
Soccer? What's that?

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:59.820
I guess they don't know about soccer.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.820
So this is the ball.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:07.730
We came up with this game.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:11.580
There's a game called kemari in the other countries that's similar to this one, though.

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:14.750
We made that ball, too.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:15.720
I see!

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.960
Hey, Tasuke! Let's keep playing!

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:19.860
Okay!

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.190
You can come join us if you want.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.450
Really? We can?

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.060
I'm Matsukaze Tenma.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.300
Nishizono Shinsuke!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.310
I'm Tasuke!

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:33.330
Well, come on!

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:35.900
Hey, wait!

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:40.750
So your family sells tofu.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.210
Yes!

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.750
Even I can make tofu.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.590
Wow, I see.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.860
Our tofu is delicious.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.710
It's pure white with just a touch of sweetness.

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:54.700
I think it's the best in our village.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.170
You must be very proud of it.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:57.790
Yes!

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:03.090
Takuto-sama, you aren't from the Owari Province, are you.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:10.340
Your hairstyle and such are peculiar, and you don't seem to know your way around the village that well.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:12.020
Oh... yeah.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:16.400
I came from a place that's completely different from here.

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:19.160
What sort of place is it like?

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:23.890
Well, it may not have scenery as beautiful as here...

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:27.420
But there was something precious there.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.470
Precious to me.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.450
Something precious...

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.640
Do you mean the person you like?

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:39.720
No, nothing like that.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.530
That's...

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:41.670
Hey, Katsu!

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:46.020
Takuto-sama's clothes have dried!

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.040
Tenma!

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:52.460
Sorry!

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.030
Don't worry about it!

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:57.630
This is kind of fun!

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:59.910
Huh? What happened to him?

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:08.940
Those are kidnappers!

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:10.190
Wait!

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:10.990
Let's go after them!

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.800
Tasuke, get down!

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:27.950
Are you okay?

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.580
Hey!

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:36.390
We'll show you what you get for angering adults!

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.360
I think we should take the whole lot 'a ya!

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:46.500
It's a big catch today!

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.380
Officers! This way!

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:49.450
What?!

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:50.840
Let's beat it!

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.090
That was close...

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.300
You kids are crazy.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.370
You saved us.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:00.960
Thank you!

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.600
Don't mention it.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.650
They're from the White Deer Gang.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:09.970
A rumor's been going around that they kidnap kids and sell them to other countries.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.700
Be careful.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.060
That's scary.

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:14.400
Why would they do that?

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:18.740
All countries are shorthanded right now due to the war.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:23.050
Children get sold off to be trained as soldiers.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.360
Selling people as if they're objects... that's horrible!

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:26.870
Tenma!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:29.600
Did something happen?

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.100
Yes, we ran into kidnappers...

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.560
But he saved us from danger.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:35.450
This man?

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.090
Yeah!

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.130
Um, uh...

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.430
I'm Kinoshita Toukichirou.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.380
Kinoshita Toukichirou?

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.350
I've heard that name before...

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.400
Kinoshita Toukichirou! Isn't that...!

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.270
Toyotomi Hideyoshi?!

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:54.570
What?

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.080
What's wrong?

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:03.150
I'm not sure I understood that, but I understand...

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:05.360
I'm sorry, it's complicated.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:11.730
Is this soccer that you're trying to bring back that much fun?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:12.990
Yes!

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:13.840
It's fun!

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:15.410
I see.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:18.530
Well, having what you love close to you is important.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:19.890
Work hard for it.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:20.460
Okay!

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:25.210
I'm working hard right now to be next to what I love most, too.

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:28.690
What is it that you love, Toukichirou-san?

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:33.110
What I love is Oda Nobunaga-sama!

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:39.970
I feel a strength from him that isn't a part of this world!

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:45.670
I can't help but feel that he'll turn be the one to turn all of the world's common practice on its head.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:50.820
You must look up to Nobunaga-sama a great deal.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:54.090
Yeah, you could say that.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.010
I'm going to be by his side one day.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:00.170
Nobunaga-sama has God-given talents.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:02.420
I know he will rule the country one day.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:04.410
Toukichirou-san...

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:08.290
If I follow him, I may become a great man, too.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.670
I am going to be great!

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.920
I will make sure of it.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.950
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:24.600
Here, Fei!

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:26.230
What's this?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.950
It's the card game!

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:31.480
Wow!

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:33.250
Wanna play?

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:34.020
Okay!

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:35.880
Here I go, Tenma!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.910
Is this really your first time?!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:40.480
Then I'll...

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:43.800
Armed!

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:47.260
This is such fun!

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:48.520
Right?!

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.940
Summer is here! The Tanabata Promo Pack Campaign!

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.980
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.530
You sure found a good stronghold.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.740
Keep the compliments coming!

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:07.940
We should start cleaning up.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.970
I found a broom here.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.700
But it's a little scary...

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:15.380
It's better than attracting unwanted attention.

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:19.630
There will be less chance of us affecting history in a place like this, too.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:24.890
Still, our pathway to Nobunaga is steep.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.640
It might not be easy.

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:29.370
It's only the first day.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:32.100
If today didn't work, there's always tomorrow.

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:37.800
Oh right, we met a person named Kinoshita Toukichirou.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:39.650
Do you know him, Fei?

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:42.570
He's the one who becomes Toyotomi Hideyoshi later on, right?

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:44.520
What?!

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:49.740
Hideyoshi is the one who unified Japan! Not even Nobunaga could do that!

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:53.660
Maybe instead of going for Nobunaga, we should go for Hideyoshi...

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:54.720
No!

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:59.460
You guys don't get it!

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:04.640
It's not the individual's ability but the players' abilities as a whole that make a team when synchronized!

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:08.670
As that unified power increases, you bring out your best performance!

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:13.520
It's as important as the combination of ingredients in the finest tasting dish.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:19.310
If you want to assemble the strongest team in history, you need the exact players that I specify...

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:22.440
...or it will NEVER happen!

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:24.530
All right...

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:30.560
Also, the one to take Nobunaga's aura will be you, Shindou Takuto.

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:32.480
It's... me?

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:38.240
Ever since I've changed into this shape, I've grown able to see the power that people possess.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:47.900
Your own special abilities as playmaker will make the most of Nobunaga's power.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:51.280
Me with Nobunaga's aura...

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.630
Shindou-senpai...

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:59.860
A gamemaker of truth who can appraise people and the general situation, while combining both stillness and motion.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.640
Shindou Takuto.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.350
That is who you will be.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:06.670
One of the strongest eleven in history.

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:07.890
Okay.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:10.300
I'll try it.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.960
I hope we find a good clue to our next step today.

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:20.330
Our big search for Nobunaga begins!

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:23.010
We can't fight on empty stomachs.

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:25.260
Let's have breakfast first.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.910
Takuto-sama!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:28.480
Okatsu-san!

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:29.130
Tasuke!

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:31.510
Tenma, this is my big sister.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.540
The two of you are siblings?

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:36.850
Um, here.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:39.030
What's this?

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:41.730
My sister made it. I guarantee it's good!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:45.790
I tried my very best to make it, as an apology for yesterday.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:48.150
I wanted Takuto-sama to try it.

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:49.530
Thank you.

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:51.580
As expected of Shindou.

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.560
I want to make a lunch box for Shin-sama too!

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:57.500
You're still as popular as ever, even in this era!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:01.290
Takuto-sama, good luck with your search!

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:02.450
Yeah!

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:09.760
That's...

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:13.330
O-Oda...

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:16.890
It's Nobunaga!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.020
What's going on?

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:27.860
Takuto-sama!

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:42.300
Wonderful!

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:45.470
Nobunaga-sama likes it...

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:47.880
You there, raise your head.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:52.010
Was it you who made these rice cakes?

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:53.120
Yes, sir.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.260
They are good.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.240
Remain adhering well to your work.

00:15:58.050 --> 00:15:59.450
Thank you!

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.700
That's Nobunaga...

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:04.490
Does he have a sweet tooth?

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:06.790
That's different from what I imagined.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.730
What's with you?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:13.610
You don't appear to be from this country.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:16.310
Well... um... we...

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:20.010
Tell me you are not Imagawa's men?

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:21.850
Absolutely not!

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.750
We're merely simple travelers.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.810
That was foolish of me.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.490
No one with a brain would name themselves an enemy.

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.140
Very well, I will believe you for now.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:43.060
Your eyes appear to be speaking the truth, besides.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.120
Nobunaga-sama!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:00.860
Out of my way!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:09.960
Wow...

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:14.970
He certainly isn't ordinary.

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:21.720
The likes of a rowdy horse is of no trouble before me.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:25.910
N-Nothing less from him.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.370
Oh, that's right!

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:33.920
What?!

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:41.520
What are those?

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:43.040
They appear to be firearms.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:46.390
T-They're called skyrocket firearms...

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:49.150
I wanted so much to show them to you, Nobunaga-sama!

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:52.530
Skyrocket firearms? They are meant for festivals?

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:55.180
Y-Yes, sir, that they are!

00:17:55.810 --> 00:18:00.350
I see. You will have to demonstrate them to me in the next festival.

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:03.410
Yes, sir, with pleasure!

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:07.380
Then adhere well to your work, fireworks craftsmen.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:09.940
He's gone.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:14.740
Still, that was a nice one calling them skyrocket fireworks.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:15.960
Care to compliment me more?

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.070
No...

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.570
Nobunaga...

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:28.700
Why didn't the Mixi-max work?

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.810
This is a first.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.900
It's a vessel issue.

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:39.630
The vessel that is Shindou could not contain Nobunaga's aura.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:43.500
That's how big and strong the aura is.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:44.930
What do you mean?

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:48.420
Both of your auras could not synchronize completely.

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:53.070
The prerequisite for Mixi-max is that both sides must be compatible.

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:59.610
What's more, the person to accept the aura must have the ability necessary to withhold it.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:04.730
But I was able to fuse with the dinosaur aura that Wondeba collected.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:10.250
That is because Nobunaga's aura is bigger and stronger than the dinosaur's.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:13.850
Not all of it can fit inside the Mixi-max gun's memory.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:20.260
Therefore, the one who is to accept its power must take it all in directly, at that very moment.

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:22.830
What should I do?

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:26.540
You must gain the ability to take in that amount of power.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.460
In other words, you have no other option but to train.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.410
Train?

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:33.840
But I don't mean normal training.

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:41.520
You must train so that you understand who Nobunaga is and are able to imagine yourself taking in a part of him.

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:46.180
Mixi-max is, after all, the fusion of two separate lives.

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:49.020
The fusion of lives...

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:50.160
I understand.

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:55.320
I'll train and succeed in Mixi-maxing with Nobunaga.

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:56.840
Well said!

00:19:56.840 --> 00:20:00.550
Now, all that's left is how to meet Nobunaga again.

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:02.270
Takuto-sama!

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:03.900
Okatsu-san!

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:06.010
What's brought you here in such a hurry?

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:10.550
You might get to meet Nobunaga-sama again!

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:13.070
I can?!

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:16.230
The village head has just notified me...

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:22.100
...that I have been chosen to serve food at the banquet for cherry blossom viewing that is being held by Nobunaga-sama.

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:24.320
Banquet for cherry blossom viewing?

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.620
That's it!

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:32.490
If we want to meet with Nobunaga, we'll have to crash this banquet!

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:37.390
And this is the plaza where the banquet is being held.

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:42.120
If we manage to sneak in here, we'll have another chance at Mixi-maxing!

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:45.150
Look, this is where Nobunaga will be sitting.

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:49.700
And the locations of the other samurai will be...

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:50.430
Katsu!

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.370
What's wrong, Mother?

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.030
Tasuke has disappeared!

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:56.030
Tasuke?!

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:59.440
Someone saw him being taken away by men.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:00.760
No way...

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:03.070
Was he kidnapped by the White Deer Gang?

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:05.520
We have to go save him!

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:07.250
But we don't know where they've taken him.

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:08.320
Oh...

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:12.950
Let's go get Toukichirou-san. He may know something.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:16.080
Right! Toukichirou-san would know!

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:23.480
Hello!

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:26.700
Give Tasuke back!

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:31.090
You're...!

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:34.090
Well...

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:38.310
Maybe I'll give him back to you if you beat us.

00:23:23.870 --> 00:23:26.130
We kickoff in the Sengoku era!

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:30.050
Tasuke, Toukichirou-san! Take a look at our soccer!

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:32.930
Next, Battle Royale! The White Deer Gang!!

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:34.760
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:44.960 --> 00:23:49.300
The Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone's proverb today is...

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:55.180
If today didn't work, there's always tomorrow.

00:23:55.180 --> 00:23:56.320
That's all!
